// Title: Allow RDP Remote Assistance Feature
// Sigma ID: 37b437cf-3fc5-4c8e-9c94-1d7c9aff842b
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-08-19 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detect enable rdp feature to allow specific user to rdp connect on the targeted machine
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the feature (alerts should be investigated either way)
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/40b77d63808dd4f4eafb83949805636735a1fd15/atomics/T1112/T1112.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_allow_rdp_remote_assistance_feature.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Terminal Server\\fAllowToGetHelp" and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)"
